## HTTP API

| Method | Path             | Purpose                                                    |
| ------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| GET    | `/`              | Embedded web UI                                            |
| GET    | `/healthz`       | Liveness (`{"status":"ok"}`)                               |
| POST   | `/v1/ocr`        | Raw image bytes in body - raw Textract OCR (synchronous)   |
| POST   | `/v1/verify`     | Multipart: `image` + `application` (or Nx`image` + `applications[]`) - `{job_id}` |
| POST   | `/v1/batch`      | JSONL body (one flat app + `image_url` per line) - `{job_id}` |
| GET    | `/v1/jobs/{id}`  | Poll a job; returns per-item criteria + overall verdict    |

`/v1/verify` and `/v1/batch` are asynchronous: they return a `job_id`, and the
client polls `/v1/jobs/{id}` until `status == "done"`.

### Application schema

`internal/model.Application` mirrors the label-matchable fields of TTB Form
5100.31, flattened (no nested objects):

```jsonc
{
  "product_type":       "distilled_spirits",   // wine | distilled_spirits | malt_beverages (required)
  "source":             "domestic",            // domestic | imported
  "brand_name":         "OLD TOM DISTILLERY",
  "applicant_name":     "Old Tom Distillery Co.",
  "applicant_address":  "Bardstown, KY",
  "class_type":         "Kentucky Straight Bourbon Whiskey",
  "alcohol_content":    "45%",
  "net_contents":       "750 mL",
  "country_of_origin":  "Scotland",
  "contains_neutral_spirits": false,
  "colored":                 false,
  "age_statement":           "",
  "state_of_distillation":   "",
  "contains_fdc_yellow5":    false,
  "contains_carmine":        false,
  "contains_sulfites":       false,
  "contains_aspartame":      false
}
```

Empty `class_type` / `alcohol_content` / `net_contents` / `country_of_origin`
mean "not asserted" (these are label-derived fields; see Assumptions below).
The boolean disclosure flags assert that the product *contains/uses* the
substance, in which case the label must carry the mandated statement.

